# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit .env — it is gitignored.
#
# The entrypoints (app/main.py, app/mcp_server.py, scripts/run_evals.py) load this file at
# startup via python-dotenv. Variables already exported in your shell always win — the file
# never overrides them, so `TRADEDESK_BROKER=alpaca uvicorn app.main:app` behaves as typed.
#
# Every switch is opt-in. With an empty .env — or none at all — the whole stack runs offline:
# mock broker, lexical retriever, keyword classifier. No key, no network.

# --- Feature switches -----------------------------------------------------------
# TRADEDESK_BROKER=alpaca routes orders to a real Alpaca PAPER account (needs the APCA_* keys
# below). Any other value, including unset, uses the offline mock broker.
TRADEDESK_BROKER=

# TRADEDESK_LLM_CLASSIFIER=1 swaps the keyword classifier for the Claude-backed one (needs
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY). Any other value stays on the offline keyword rules.
TRADEDESK_LLM_CLASSIFIER=

# TRADEDESK_RETRIEVER=chroma swaps lexical BM25 for embedding retrieval (ChromaRetriever).
# The Chroma default embedder downloads model weights on FIRST startup — do that before the
# demo, not during it. Any other value stays lexical and offline.
TRADEDESK_RETRIEVER=

# TRADEDESK_MCP_ROLE=compliance starts the MCP server read-only; any other value, including
# unset, starts it as the trading persona. (MCP server only — the chat UI takes the role per
# session via POST /api/session.)
TRADEDESK_MCP_ROLE=

# Cap on concurrently stored chat sessions; least-recently-used sessions are evicted past it.
# Unset means the default (500). The endpoint is unauthenticated, so this bound is what keeps
# a session-creation loop from exhausting memory.
TRADEDESK_MAX_SESSIONS=

# --- Alpaca: PAPER TRADING ONLY -------------------------------------------------
# Generate at https://app.alpaca.markets/paper/dashboard/overview
#
# The base URL is HARD-CODED to paper-api.alpaca.markets in app/brokerage/alpaca.py — there is
# deliberately no setting that can point this app at the live-money API. But Alpaca uses the
# same key format for live and paper accounts, so a live key pasted here would authenticate
# against the paper host and quietly mix credentials across environments. If you ever hold
# live credentials, keep them in a separate profile entirely — they have no business in this
# project.
APCA_API_KEY_ID=
APCA_API_SECRET_KEY=

# --- LLM ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed for TRADEDESK_LLM_CLASSIFIER=1. The offline demo runs without it.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Model for the LLM classifier. Unset means the default (claude-opus-4-8).
MODEL_ID=
